Day 05 of my bug bounty series: understanding authentication.

Login pages look simple. Behind them is where a lot of serious bugs live.

Today I learned 4 things:

1. Authentication: how a user proves who they are.
2. Authorization: what that user is allowed to do. It's not the same thing as authentication.
3. Sessions: a session ID is how the site remembers you after login.
4. Cookies: where that session ID usually sits, along with preferences.

Mixing up authentication and authorization is one of the most common beginner mistakes. I did it too.

